Annotations: |
  This cell declares a designed, swappable extension point: `BillingApi` is the app-facing
  contract for an in-app-purchase backend, with a default no-op Empty implementation declared
  right on the interface. Which concrete implementation backs it at runtime (a real Google Play
  Billing client, or the Empty no-op) is decided outside this cell, by whichever build flavor
  wires up AppDependencies (see dependencies cell).

---

"BillingApi()":
  location: BillingApi.kt
  annotations: |
    Contract for an in-app-purchase backend: querying product pricing, querying/observing
    purchase state, and launching the platform purchase flow. Every method has a default no-op
    body, so a build variant with no billing backend at all can use the nested Empty object
    without writing any code.
  methods:
    "getBillingPurchaseResults() -> stream:Flow<BillingPurchaseResult>": |
      A stream of purchase-result updates. Callers must call queryPurchases after subscribing
      to trigger an initial check; this stream does not query eagerly on its own.
    "getApiAvailability() -> code:BillingResponseCode": |
      Whether the platform billing API is currently usable on this device.
    "queryProduct() -> product:BillingProduct?": |
      The current pricing for the app's single subscribable product, or none if unavailable.
      Implementations are expected to cache this for roughly 24 hours.
    "queryPurchases() -> result:BillingPurchaseResult": |
      Checks the user's current purchase state and also propagates the result through
      getBillingPurchaseResults.
    "launchBillingFlow(activity: Activity)": |
      Starts the platform's purchase UI flow for the app's product.

"BillingDependencies()":
  location: BillingDependencies.kt
  annotations: |
    The dependency contract a `BillingApi` implementation needs from its host app: application
    context and the identifiers of the specific product/plan being sold. Kept separate from
    `BillingApi` itself so the interface stays swappable independent of how those values are
    sourced (e.g. from a remotely-configured donations configuration object).
  properties:
    "context -> Context": |
      Application context.
  methods:
    "getProductId() -> id:String": |
      The billing-platform product id to query/purchase.
    "getBasePlanId() -> id:String": |
      The billing-platform base-plan id within that product.

"BillingPurchaseResult()":
  location: BillingPurchaseResult.kt
  annotations: |
    Sealed result of a purchase query or purchase-flow attempt: Success (with purchase state,
    token, and renewal info), or one of several named non-success outcomes (UserCancelled,
    None, TryAgainLater, AlreadySubscribed, FeatureNotSupported, GenericError,
    NetworkError, BillingUnavailable).

"BillingResponseCode()":
  location: BillingResponseCode.kt
  annotations: |
    Enumerates the platform billing library's response codes (OK, USER_CANCELED,
    SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE, BILLING_UNAVAILABLE, ITEM_UNAVAILABLE, DEVELOPER_ERROR, ERROR,
    ITEM_ALREADY_OWNED, ITEM_NOT_OWNED, NETWORK_ERROR, plus UNKNOWN/SERVICE_TIMEOUT/
    FEATURE_NOT_SUPPORTED/SERVICE_DISCONNECTED for this app's own edge cases), each carrying
    the platform's raw integer code.
  properties:
    "isSuccess -> Boolean": |
      True only for OK.

"BillingProduct(price: FiatMoney)":
  location: BillingProduct.kt
  annotations: |
    A purchasable product's current price.

    `price`: the product's price, in the currency the billing platform reports for the current
    user/region.

"BillingPurchaseState()":
  location: BillingPurchaseState.kt
  annotations: |
    Enumerates a purchase's platform-reported state: UNSPECIFIED, PURCHASED, or PENDING.

"BillingError(billingResponseCode: Int)":
  location: BillingError.kt
  annotations: |
    Exception thrown by a `BillingApi` implementation when a platform billing call fails.

    `billingResponseCode`: the platform's raw response code for the failure.

